{
  "duration": 81.479,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.119,
      "end": 0.259,
      "text": "So,"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.74,
      "end": 1.559,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.259,
      "end": 4.139,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.619,
      "end": 7.679,
      "text": "Now, in this problem, the boat's still water speed is"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.099,
      "end": 9.399,
      "text": "ten kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.96,
      "end": 11.8,
      "text": "The stream speed is two kilometers per hour,"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.439,
      "end": 17.139,
      "text": "and the distance for both upstream and downstream journeys is twenty-four kilometer."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.699,
      "end": 22.859,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find how much more time the upstream journey takes than the downstream journey."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.459,
      "end": 25.559,
      "text": "Let us first recall the basic formulas."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.039,
      "end": 28.439,
      "text": "When the boat moves against the stream,"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.859,
      "end": 30.179,
      "text": "the stream slows it down."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.739,
      "end": 35.999,
      "text": "So upstream speed equals boat speed minus stream speed equals ten minus two"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.599,
      "end": 38.219,
      "text": "equals eight kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.7,
      "end": 40.779,
      "text": "When the boat moves with the stream,"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.159,
      "end": 42.999,
      "text": "the stream helps it move faster."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.459,
      "end": 50.139,
      "text": "So downstream speed equals boat speed plus stream speed equals ten plus two equals twelve kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.759,
      "end": 51.039,
      "text": "Done."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.759,
      "end": 54.399,
      "text": "Now we know both speeds, so finding the time becomes easy."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.86,
      "end": 58.479,
      "text": "We use the formula time equals distance divided by speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.139,
      "end": 67.459,
      "text": "Upstream time equals twenty-four divided by eight equals three hours, and downstream time equals twenty-four divided by twelve equals two hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.919,
      "end": 70.219,
      "text": "Now, the question is not asking for the individual times."
    },
    {
      "start": 70.619,
      "end": 73.799,
      "text": "It is asking how much more time the upstream journey takes."
    },
    {
      "start": 74.139,
      "end": 76.639,
      "text": "So difference equals three minus two equals one hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.379,
      "end": 81.479,
      "text": "Hence, the required answer is one hour. So the correct answer is option A."
    }
  ],
